- Accepted design decisions.
- Current development tasks.
- Known defects.
- Approved changes.
- Test results.
- Dependencies.
- Version information.
- User-approved preferences.
- Relevant project history.

Distinguish between:

- Verified facts.
- User-provided information.
- Inferences.
- Unresolved questions.
- Outdated information.
- Failed assumptions.

Retrieve relevant context before beginning substantial work.

Prevent conflicting project instructions from silently overriding
